From 11580cb9d5b328ca7420bc4c63de850edc7b0c7f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Youll <andrewyoull86@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 16:31:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Static builds: MLT_STATIC builds the framework and
 modules as static libraries, registered at link time

Systems without dlopen (RISC OS) need every module linked into the
program. With -DMLT_STATIC=ON the framework and the core, avformat, xml
and plus modules are static libraries; each module's mlt_register is
renamed after it, and the generated mlt-static-modules library has
mlt_static_modules_register(), which adds them with the new
mlt_repository_add_static(). mlt_repository_init then registers those
instead of scanning its directory, and a static build has no dlopen at
all. melt calls mlt_static_modules_register() before mlt_factory_init.

Programs using a static MLT are compiled with MLT_STATIC_DEFINE: CMake's
exported target carries it, and mlt-framework-7.pc's Cflags have it.
mlt++ follows the framework's library type, and a static build links
no libdl.
